# The largest quantum a composed layer can carry, where the set admits one. One row per composed
# layer every one of whose parts is lumpy: the greatest common divisor of the parts' quanta, each
# converted into the composed layer's unit by its part's factor, and why there is none where there
# is none.
#
# Every attainable sum is a multiple of the gcd
#   Each part's nameplate is a whole number of its own quanta, so a composed nameplate is a sum
#   `a1 q1 + a2 q2 + ...` with every `a` a whole number of units held. Every such sum is a multiple
#   of `g = gcd(q1, q2, ...)`, and no larger number divides them all, so `g` is the quantum the
#   composed supply still arrives in. Bézout says every multiple of `g` is `a1 q1 + a2 q2` for some
#   integers, but a count of units held is never negative: over the counts a supply can actually
#   hold, the attainable sums are a numerical semigroup, all multiples of `g` without being all
#   of them. `q = 4` and `q = 6` can never make 2. Proof: `src/proofs/README.md`, entry
#   `composed_quantum`.
#
# A single layer has no best quantum
#   Asking for a "best" quantum of a single layer is the wrong question. There the divisor set of
#   `n` is never empty (1 and `n` are always in it), so existence decides nothing, and the quantum
#   is observed rather than chosen: it is the indivisible unit supply arrives in. The question only
#   becomes well posed over a set of parts, where the intersection can be narrower than any one
#   divisor set and is what the composition actually admits.
#
# Converted first, as every other quantity is
#   A conversion factor multiplies a quantum like any other figure in the part's unit, so each
#   quantum is converted into the composed layer's unit before the fold: `8 GPU` at
#   `720 GPU-hour per GPU` is `5760 GPU-hour`, and folds with a `720 GPU-hour` quantum to 720. A
#   part with no factor keeps its own unit, which is the composed layer's wherever
#   checks/unit_crossing_without_a_factor passes.
#
# The mode of a factor with width
#   A factor with width converts a quantum into a range of quanta, and a gcd of ranges is not
#   one number. The fold reads each factor at its mode, as the calendar's 720 hours is read, and
#   `spread` says the answer rests on that reading.
#
# Why there is no quantum, as a typed absence
#   `unmeasured` where some part's factor is: nobody sized the conversion, so nobody can say what
#   the parts share. `notApplicable` where the converted quanta still sit in different units:
#   divisibility is a relation on one ordered set, and two quanta in different units have no
#   common divisor to find. A NULL alone would not say which.
#
# Every part as filed, not every part that resolves
#   "Every one of whose parts is lumpy" counts the parts the fusion names, from
#   composition/part_references.sqlc. A part that is not here has a quantum nobody can read, and a
#   gcd over the parts that remain is a multiple of the true one, so it would state a quantum the
#   composed supply need not arrive in. Such a fusion has no row, as one with a continuous part has
#   none; composition/unresolved_parts.sqlc names the part.
#
# `q = 1` is a real answer
#   Every integer is a multiple of 1, so the constraint is vacuous and the composed supply is
#   continuous for all the arithmetic can tell. Saying so is more useful than declining to answer.
#
# The fold is recursive because gcd has no aggregate
#   gcd(a,b,c) = gcd(gcd(a,b),c) is associative, so the order of the fold is immaterial; the
#   ordering below exists only to make the recursion terminate, not to choose an answer.
-- composition/parts.sqlc against layers/lumpy.sqlc, converted by asrt:factor and folded by gcd, over every part in composition/part_references.sqlc.
WITH RECURSIVE base AS (
    SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer,
           CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'stated' THEN c.n_unit ELSE l.quantum_unit END AS quantum_unit,
           CASE WHEN p.factor_state IN ('omitted', 'stated')
                THEN l.quantum_mode * coalesce(p.factor_mode, 1) END             AS quantum_mode,
           coalesce(p.factor_low <> p.factor_high, false)                         AS spread,
           p.factor_absent, p.factor_derivation
    FROM      (
        :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
    ) p
    JOIN      (
        :compose(layers/lumpy.sqlc)
    ) l ON l.filing = p.part_filing AND l.layer = p.part_layer
    LEFT JOIN (
        :compose(layers/nameplate.sqlc)
    ) c ON c.filing = p.composition AND c.layer = p.composed_layer
    WHERE l.quantum_mode > 0
),
every_part AS (
    SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer, p.parts
    FROM (
        :compose(folds/fusion_parts.sqlc)
    ) p
),
shape AS (
    SELECT composition, composed_layer,
           count(*)                                         AS lumpy_parts,
           count(quantum_mode)                              AS sized,
           count(DISTINCT quantum_unit)                     AS units,
           min(quantum_unit)                                AS unit,
           bool_or(spread)                                  AS spread,
           min(factor_absent)                               AS unsized,
           min(factor_derivation)                           AS unsized_by
    FROM base GROUP BY composition, composed_layer
),
ordered AS (
    SELECT b.*, row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY b.composition, b.composed_layer
                                   ORDER BY b.quantum_unit, b.quantum_mode) AS i
    FROM base b
    WHERE b.quantum_mode IS NOT NULL
),
fold AS (
    SELECT composition, composed_layer, i, quantum_mode AS g FROM ordered WHERE i = 1
  UNION ALL
    SELECT o.composition, o.composed_layer, o.i, gcd(f.g, o.quantum_mode)
    FROM fold f
    JOIN ordered o ON o.composition    = f.composition
                  AND o.composed_layer = f.composed_layer
                  AND o.i              = f.i + 1
)
SELECT s.composition, s.composed_layer, e.parts, s.units, s.spread,
       CASE WHEN s.unsized IS NULL AND s.unsized_by IS NULL AND s.units = 1 THEN s.unit END
           AS unit,
       CASE WHEN s.unsized IS NULL AND s.unsized_by IS NULL AND s.units = 1 THEN f.g END
           AS composed_quantum,
       CASE WHEN s.unsized IS NOT NULL THEN s.unsized
            WHEN s.unsized_by IS NULL AND s.units > 1 THEN 'notApplicable'::pm.absence_reason END
           AS absent,
       s.unsized_by AS factor_derivation
FROM      shape      s
JOIN      every_part e ON e.composition = s.composition
                      AND e.composed_layer = s.composed_layer
                      AND e.parts = s.lumpy_parts
LEFT JOIN fold       f ON f.composition = s.composition
                      AND f.composed_layer = s.composed_layer
                      AND f.i = s.sized
